    <briefdescription>
<para>Exports ThemisDB process instances as OCEL 2.0 JSON event logs. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Enables import into external process mining tools (PM4Py, Celonis, ProM) for advanced analytics: object-centric discovery, conformance checking, and process enhancement.</para>
<para>Object types are derived from <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1process_1_1_process_linker" kindref="compound">ProcessLinker</ref></computeroutput> attachment collections. Events are derived from <computeroutput>ProcessToken::visited_nodes</computeroutput> and their timestamps stored in <computeroutput>ProcessToken::visit_timestamps</computeroutput>.</para>
<para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="classthemis_1_1process_1_1_ocel_exporter_1a333f3c03577195417230c9b62f0b4826" kindref="member">OcelExporter</ref><sp/>exp(db,<sp/>engine,<sp/>models,<sp/>linker);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>log<sp/>=<sp/>exp.exportInstance(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;bauantrag-inst-001&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>log<sp/>is<sp/>OCEL<sp/>2.0<sp/>JSON<sp/>—<sp/>ready<sp/>for<sp/>PM4Py::ocel.read_ocel2_json()</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
